# Frontend Coding Standards

Version: 1.0

Last Updated: 2026-06-26

Status: Active

---

# Purpose

This document defines frontend code quality expectations, naming conventions, component structure, hooks, styling, TypeScript, testing, performance, and accessibility patterns for TypeScript, JavaScript, and Vue applications.

This document governs:

* developer_frontend
* architect_frontend
* code_reviewer
* debugger
* unit_test_writer

(when scope is frontend — `**/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx,vue}` or frontend TODO file scope)

All frontend implementation work must comply with this standard unless explicitly overridden by an approved ADR.

Universal quality rules (code review, refactoring, traceability, debugging) remain in `coding-standards.mdc`.

Full section index: `.cursor/rules-index.md` -> `standards-frontend.mdc`.

---

# Precedence

When rules conflict, higher-priority sources win:

```text
agent-governance.mdc → coding-standards.mdc → standards-frontend.mdc → tech-stack-frontend.mdc
```

`coding-standards.mdc` owns universal review, refactoring, and traceability rules. This document owns frontend-specific code quality. `tech-stack-frontend.mdc` owns approved technologies and tool-specific implementation patterns.

