# Naming Conventions

## File Naming

| Type | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Components | PascalCase | `UserProfile.tsx`, `ButtonGroup.tsx` |
| Hooks | camelCase with `use` prefix | `useApiClient.ts`, `useLocalStorage.ts` |
| Utils | camelCase | `formatDate.ts`, `validateEmail.ts` |
| Types / Interfaces | PascalCase | `User.types.ts`, `ApiResponse.types.ts` |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for values; camelCase for files | `API_ENDPOINTS.ts` |
| Config files | camelCase with `Config` suffix | `formConfig.ts`, `tableConfig.ts` |
| Styles | kebab-case | `button-styles.css` |
| Test files | `[name].test.ts(x)` | `Button.test.tsx`, `useCounter.test.ts` |

## Variables and Functions

Preferred:

```typescript
const userData: UserData = {};
const isLoading = false;
const hasError = false;
const handleSubmit = () => {};
const fetchUserData = async () => {};
```

Avoid:

```typescript
const user_data = {};     // snake_case
const loading = false;    // ambiguous boolean prefix
const onClick = () => {}; // event handler is too generic
const getData = async () => {}; // too vague
```

## Constants

```typescript
const MAX_RETRY_COUNT = 3;
const DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 30;
const API_BASE_URL = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL!;
```

