# Styling Standards

Tailwind CSS with `cn()` utility is the preferred approach — see `tech-stack-frontend.mdc` -> Styling Standard for tool selection policy.

## cn() Utility

```typescript
import { clsx, type ClassValue } from 'clsx';
import { twMerge } from 'tailwind-merge';

export function cn(...inputs: ClassValue[]) {
  return twMerge(clsx(inputs));
}
```

## Tailwind Class Order

1. Layout (`flex`, `grid`, `block`)
2. Sizing (`w-full`, `h-screen`)
3. Spacing (`p-4`, `m-2`, `gap-3`)
4. Typography (`text-sm`, `font-bold`)
5. Visual (`bg-primary`, `rounded-md`)
6. Interactive (`hover:bg-secondary`, `focus:ring-2`)
7. State (`disabled:opacity-50`)

## Conditional Classes

```typescript
// Good
<button className={cn(
  'flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2',
  'bg-primary text-white rounded-md',
  'hover:bg-primary/90 focus:ring-2',
  variant === 'danger' && 'bg-red-500 hover:bg-red-600',
  className
)}>
```

## Avoid

```typescript
// Bad: Hard-to-read inline class strings
<div className="p-4 m-2 bg-blue-500 hover:bg-blue-600 text-white font-bold py-2 px-4 rounded shadow-lg transform transition-transform hover:scale-105">

// Good: Extract to variable
const buttonClasses = cn(
  'py-2 px-4 rounded font-bold text-white',
  'bg-blue-500 hover:bg-blue-600',
  'shadow-lg transform transition-transform hover:scale-105'
);
```

## Responsive Design

Use mobile-first approach:

```typescript
<div className="
  w-full md:w-1/2 lg:w-1/3
  p-4 md:p-6 lg:p-8
">
```

