# Testing Standards

Test framework selection (Vitest or Jest, React Testing Library, MSW) is defined in `tech-stack-frontend.mdc` -> Testing Standard and Enterprise Capability Baseline.

## Test File Location

Preferred: co-located with the source file.

```text
├── Button.tsx
└── Button.test.tsx
```

Allowed: separate tests folder.

```text
tests/
├── unit/
│   └── Button.test.tsx
└── integration/
    └── checkout-flow.test.ts
```

## Component Testing

```typescript
import { render, screen, fireEvent } from '@testing-library/react';
import { describe, it, expect, vi } from 'vitest';
import { Button } from './Button';

describe('Button', () => {
  it('renders with correct text', () => {
    render(<Button>Click me</Button>);
    expect(screen.getByText('Click me')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  it('handles click events', () => {
    const handleClick = vi.fn();
    render(<Button onClick={handleClick}>Click me</Button>);
    fireEvent.click(screen.getByText('Click me'));
    expect(handleClick).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);
  });

  it('is disabled when loading', () => {
    render(<Button disabled>Click me</Button>);
    expect(screen.getByRole('button')).toBeDisabled();
  });
});
```

## Hook Testing

```typescript
import { renderHook, act } from '@testing-library/react';
import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest';
import { useCounter } from './useCounter';

describe('useCounter', () => {
  it('increments correctly', () => {
    const { result } = renderHook(() => useCounter({ initial: 0 }));
    act(() => { result.current.increment(); });
    expect(result.current.count).toBe(1);
  });
});
```

## Test Requirements

- Tests must be independent and repeatable
- Tests must cover happy path, error states, edge cases, and loading states
- Use `vi.fn()` (Vitest) or `jest.fn()` (Jest) for mock functions — never real implementations in unit tests
- Use MSW for API mocking in integration tests
- Coverage target: 80% or higher (guideline, not a quality guarantee)

