# Performance Guidelines

Optimization policy (lazy loading, code splitting, bundle awareness) is defined in `tech-stack-frontend.mdc` -> Performance Standard. Below are implementation patterns.

## Memoization

```typescript
// Memoize expensive computations
const sortedData = useMemo(() => {
  return [...data].sort((a, b) => a.score - b.score);
}, [data]);

// Memoize callbacks passed to children
const handleUpdate = useCallback((id: string) => {
  updateItem(id, { updated: true });
}, [updateItem]);

// Memoize components rendered in lists or as children
export const ListItem = memo(function ListItem({ item }: { item: Item }) {
  return <div>{item.name}</div>;
});
```

## Lazy Loading

```typescript
// Lazy load routes
const Dashboard = lazy(() => import('./pages/Dashboard'));

// Lazy load heavy components
const HeavyChart = lazy(() => import('./components/HeavyChart'));
```

## Image Optimization

```typescript
// Use next/image for all images
import Image from 'next/image';

<Image
  src="/photo.jpg"
  alt="Descriptive alt text"
  width={800}
  height={600}
  priority={isAboveFold}
  placeholder="blur"
/>
```

Prohibited:

- Raw `<img>` tags for user-facing content
- Importing entire libraries when tree-shakeable alternatives exist
- Premature optimization without measurement

