# Accessibility Standards

WCAG 2.1 Level AA policy is defined in `tech-stack-frontend.mdc` -> Accessibility Standard. Below are implementation patterns.

## Accessible Components

```typescript
// Good: Accessible button with icon
<button
  type="button"
  aria-label="Close dialog"
  aria-pressed={isOpen}
  onClick={onClose}
>
  <XIcon aria-hidden="true" />
</button>

// Good: Accessible form field
<label htmlFor="email">Email Address</label>
<input
  id="email"
  type="email"
  aria-required="true"
  aria-invalid={hasError}
  aria-describedby={hasError ? 'email-error' : undefined}
/>
{hasError && (
  <span id="email-error" role="alert">{error}</span>
)}
```

## Prohibited

- Interactive controls without keyboard access
- Icon-only actions without `aria-label`
- Relying on color alone to convey meaning
- Modals that trap focus without a close mechanism

