# Comments and Documentation

## When to Comment

Comment to explain **why**, not **what**.

```typescript
// Good: Explains why
// Defer heavy calculation to avoid blocking the initial render
const deferredValue = useDeferredValue(heavyData);

// Bad: Explains what (obvious)
// Set count to 0
setCount(0);
```

## JSDoc for Public APIs

```typescript
/**
 * Formats a date to locale string.
 * @param date - Date to format
 * @param locale - Optional locale string (defaults to 'id-ID')
 * @returns Formatted date string
 * @example
 * formatDate(new Date()) // '17 Juni 2024'
 */
export function formatDate(date: Date, locale = 'id-ID'): string {
  return date.toLocaleDateString(locale, {
    year: 'numeric',
    month: 'long',
    day: 'numeric',
  });
}
```

