# Security Standards

Browser storage, CSP, and cross-site risk policy are defined in `tech-stack-frontend.mdc` -> Security Standard (Frontend) and `tech-stack-security.mdc`. Below are implementation patterns.

## Input Validation

```typescript
// Good: Validate all inputs with Zod
const loginSchema = z.object({
  email: z.string().email('Invalid email'),
  password: z.string().min(8, 'Password must be at least 8 characters'),
});

const result = loginSchema.safeParse(data);
if (!result.success) {
  return { error: result.error };
}
```

## HTML Sanitization

```typescript
// Good: Sanitize HTML before rendering
import DOMPurify from 'dompurify';

function RichText({ html }: { html: string }) {
  const sanitized = DOMPurify.sanitize(html);
  return <div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: sanitized }} />;
}
```

## Data Handling

```typescript
// Bad: Never log sensitive data
console.log('User data:', user); // may contain password

// Good: Selective safe logging
const { password, accessToken, ...safeUser } = user;
console.log('User data:', safeUser);
```

Prohibited:

- Logging passwords, tokens, secrets, or sensitive personal data
- Using `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without sanitization

