# Code Review Checklist

## Functionality

- [ ] Feature meets the requirement
- [ ] Error handling is implemented
- [ ] Edge cases are handled
- [ ] Loading states are explicit
- [ ] Empty states are handled

## Code Quality

- [ ] TypeScript types are complete (no unresolved `any`)
- [ ] Functions are focused and not too long (< 50 lines ideally)
- [ ] No duplicated code (DRY)
- [ ] Naming is clear and descriptive
- [ ] Export style is correct (named, not default for components)

## Performance

- [ ] Memoization used for expensive computations and callbacks to children
- [ ] Images use `next/image`
- [ ] No unnecessary re-renders
- [ ] Bundle size is considered

## Testing

- [ ] Unit tests cover business logic
- [ ] Component tests cover UI behavior
- [ ] Edge cases are tested
- [ ] Tests pass in CI

## Security

- [ ] All inputs validated with Zod
- [ ] HTML output sanitized where applicable
- [ ] No secrets in code
- [ ] Authentication checks present

## Accessibility

- [ ] Keyboard navigation works
- [ ] Focus management is correct
- [ ] ARIA attributes are present and correct
- [ ] Color is not the only indicator of meaning

